Campfire for BEAM (iOS only): a CMake option that builds wallet-api as an
in-process static library.

iOS does not let an app start child processes, so the BEAM core cannot run there as
the wallet-api executable Campfire uses on the desktop and Android. With
-DBEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY=ON -DBEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY_SOURCE=<file> this adds the
static library target beam_wallet_api_lib, compiled from Campfire's
scripts/beam/core/ios/src/api_cli_library.cpp. That file includes
wallet/api/cli/api_cli.cpp with main() renamed and exports the C interface in
scripts/beam/core/ios/src/beam_wallet_api.h (beam_wallet_api_run/stop/...).

This patch touches one existing file and adds no source to the BEAM tree.
scripts/beam/core/ios applies it after the core series (../patches); the desktop
and Android builds never see it. It is also inert on its own: the option defaults
to OFF, and without it wallet/api/CMakeLists.txt defines exactly the stock targets.
api_cli.cpp is not edited (its log macros embed __LINE__).

For tag beam-7.5.14493 + the core series, patch -p1.

--- a/wallet/api/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/wallet/api/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -115,4 +115,28 @@
             COMMAND ${CMAKE_COMMAND} -E copy ${IPFS_DLL} ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}
         )
     endif()
-endif()
\ No newline at end of file
+endif()
+
+# Campfire for BEAM (iOS patch 0101): wallet-api as a static library with a C
+# entry point, for platforms where the app may not start a child process (iOS).
+# Its one source file is Campfire's (scripts/beam/core/ios/src/api_cli_library.cpp),
+# passed in as BEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY_SOURCE; it compiles cli/api_cli.cpp with
+# main() renamed. Off by default: without the option this file defines exactly
+# the stock targets.
+option(BEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY "Build beam_wallet_api_lib: wallet-api's main() as beam_wallet_api_run()" OFF)
+if (BEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY)
+    if (NOT BEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY_SOURCE OR NOT EXISTS "${BEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY_SOURCE}")
+        message(FATAL_ERROR "BEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY=ON needs BEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY_SOURCE=<path of api_cli_library.cpp>")
+    endif()
+    add_library(beam_wallet_api_lib STATIC "${BEAM_WALLET_API_LIBRARY_SOURCE}")
+    if (BEAM_ATOMIC_SWAP_SUPPORT)
+        target_sources(beam_wallet_api_lib PRIVATE cli/api_cli_swap.cpp)
+    endif()
+    target_link_libraries(beam_wallet_api_lib
+        PUBLIC
+            wallet_api
+            http
+            cli
+            mnemonic
+    )
+endif()
